      <div class="kicker reveal">What To Do Next</div>
      <h2 class="reveal">Actionable takeaways heading into 2025</h2>
      <div class="panel reveal">
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li><strong>Adopt component ownership where differentiation matters:</strong> shadcn/ui pattern outperformed packaged abstraction.</li>
          <li><strong>Re-evaluate HTML-first architectures:</strong> htmx growth indicates mainstream appetite for simpler frontends.</li>
          <li><strong>Plan React strategy at framework layer:</strong> treat React 19 primitives as a spec interpreted by tools.</li>
          <li><strong>Assume AI integration baseline:</strong> AI-capable workflows are now expected in developer-facing products.</li>
          <li><strong>Track Vue ecosystem velocity:</strong> rising UI libraries + reactivity work point to durable optionality in 2025.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="footer reveal">2025 lens: optimize for ownership, interoperability, and AI-native workflows</div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <script>
    const slides = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.slide'));
    const io = new IntersectionObserver((entries)=>{
